Synthesis of \(\mathbf{L_{B}}^{3}{-}\mathbf{Zr_{3}}^{8}{-}f\pmb{u}\) (10, BUT-97): A solution of \(\mathrm{H}_{4}\mathrm{L}_{\mathrm{B}}{}^{3}\) \((5~\mathrm{mg},~0.03~\mathrm{mmol})\) , \(\mathrm{ZrCl_{4}}\) \((20~\mathrm{mg},~0.11~\mathrm{mmol})\) , and acetic acid \((0.3\,\mathrm{\mL})\) in \(2\,\textrm{m L}\) of DMF was generated and sealed in a \(5~\mathrm{mL}\) glass vial. Then the vial was placed into an oven and heated to \(120~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for 48 hours followed by cooling to \(25~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) at a rate of \(0.5\ ^{\circ}\mathrm{C}/\) minute. The resulting colorless crystals were collected by suction filtration, washed with DMF \((50\;\mathrm{mL})\) and acetone \((50\;\mathrm{mL})\) , in turn, for three times at room temperature, and then dried in air \((4.0\;\mathrm{mg})\).
Synthesis of \(\mathbf{L_{C}}^{2}{-}\mathbf{Zr_{1}}^{12}{-}f\pmb{c}\pmb{u}\) (12, BUT-98): A solution of \(\mathrm{H}_{4}\mathrm{L}_{\mathrm{C}}{}^{2}\) \((10~\mathrm{mg},~0.034~\mathrm{mmol})\) , \(\mathrm{ZrCl_{4}}\) \((20~\mathrm{mg},~0.11~\mathrm{mmol})\) , and formic acid \((0.10~\mathrm{mL})\) in \(10~\mathrm{mL}\) of DMF/NMP \((1.5/0.5\,\mathrm{\mL})\) was generated and sealed in a \(20~\mathrm{mL}\) glass vial. Then the vial was placed into an oven and heated to \(120~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for 48 hours followed by cooling to \(25~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) at a rate of \(0.5\ ^{\circ}\mathrm{C}/\) minute. The resulting colorless crystals were collected by suction filtration, washed NMP \((50\;\mathrm{mL})\) and acetone \((50\;\mathrm{mL})\) , in turn, for three times at room temperature, and then dried in air \((8.0\;\mathrm{mg})\).
Sample Activation and Gas Sorption. In each case, the as-synthesized samples (about \(100~\mathrm{~mg})\) obtained through solvothermal synthesis were immersed in fresh DMF \((30\;\mathrm{mL})\) at \(60~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for \(24~\mathrm{h}\) to remove all unreacted starting materials. After two additional solvent exchanges in acetone \((50\;\mathrm{mL})\) for \(24~\mathrm{h}\) each, the samples were then collected and activated at \(40\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) under vacuum for \(12~\mathrm{h}\). It should be noted that \(\mathrm{L_{A}}^{1}{-}\mathrm{Zr_{6}}^{8}{-}f\pmb{u}\) (1) and \(\mathrm{L_{B}}^{1}{-}\mathrm{Zr_{6}}^{8}{-}f\pmb{u}\) (7) were first activated by supercritical \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\). The \(\mathrm{N}_{2}\) sorption experiments were recorded at \(77\,\mathrm{K}\).
PXRD Measurements. The activated samples (about 10 mg in each) were immersed in about \(3\,\mathrm{~mL~}\) of aqueous solutions in a dynamic range of \(\mathrm{pH}\) utilizing HCl and NaOH. Each of the solutions were prepared with HCl and NaOH to achieve the ideal \(\mathrm{pH}\) for the study. Each sample was immersed in each of the aqueous solutions at room temperature for \(24~\mathrm{h}\). The PXRD patterns were then recorded after collection of the samples by filtration.
\(\mathbf{N}_{2}\) Sorption Stability Tests. Activated samples of the MOFs (about \(100~\mathrm{mg}\)) were immersed in \(35~\mathrm{mL}\) of aqueous solution for \(24~\mathrm{h}\). These solutions were prepared in a dynamic range of \(\mathrm{pH}\) utilizing HCl and NaOH. The samples were then immersed in \(200\,\mathrm{~mL~}\) of acetone at \(40\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for \(12\,\mathrm{~h~}\). After filtration and subsequent air drying, the samples were activated at \(100\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for \(10~\mathrm{h}\) before the \(\mathrm{N}_{2}\) sorption experiments were conducted at \(77\,\mathrm{K}\).
